    "headline": "Special Weather Statement issued October 22 at 1:33PM PDT by NWS Los Angeles/Oxnard CA",
    "description": "At 133 PM PDT, Doppler radar was tracking a strong thunderstorm over\nWest Covina, moving east at 15 mph.\n\nHAZARD...Wind gusts of 50 to 55 mph and half inch hail. There\nis a small chance for a brief, weak tornado.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around\nunsecured objects. Minor hail damage to vegetation is\npossible.\n\nLocations impacted include...\nSan Dimas...\nGlendora...\nWest Covina...\nPomona...\nLa Verne...\nCovina...\nAzusa...\nWalnut...\nand Irwindale.",
    "instruction": "If outdoors, consider seeking shelter inside a building.\n\nBe aware of torrential rainfall.",
